# PLAT-36's Vim-configuration corpus. These are UPSTREAM BYTES, pinned by
# SHA-256 in `provenance.tsv`, and the partition law's denominator is a
# property of them. A checkout that normalised their line endings would change
# every digest and would silently change `mapLines` for any file whose
# continuation lines the rewrite touched — so nothing may touch them. This is
# PLAT-24's `.gitattributes` one directory over, for the same reason.
*.vim -text -diff
*.tsv -text
